.export-meta.is-declined {
  color: #ffcc00;
  flex-basis: 100%;
  line-height: 1.6;
  max-width: 100%;
}

/* THE NON-ANSWER THAT COULD NOT BE ASKED.

   GRID -, SUB - and NO MAP are drawn in the same bordered boxes as MAP, NEWS
   and COPY ID, so they read as buttons; each one held its reason in a title
   attribute, and a phone reports hover: none. On this cut 4,633 of 7,680 rows
   carry the dashes and 26 carry NO MAP. The chips are now tappable and print
   their own reason on its own line in the cell.

   flex-basis: 100% because .project-actions is a wrapping flex row: without it
   the sentence would be squeezed between two chips, which is the failure the
   export refusal above already had to fix. */

.action-metric[title], .action-disabled[title] {
  cursor: pointer;
}

.action-explain {
  flex: 1 0 100%;
  margin: 5px 0 2px;
  padding: 7px 9px;
  background: #07090c;
  border: 1px solid #37404a;
  border-left: 3px solid #5fbdc2;
  color: #c8d0d8;
  font: 400 10px/1.55 'Courier New', monospace;
  text-transform: none;
}

/* A coarse pointer has no hover to fall back on, so the chip that carries the
   only explanation has to be reachable by a thumb. 44px is the same floor the
   technology row and the wider-fleet select already meet. */
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  .action-metric[title], .action-disabled[title] {
    min-height: 44px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
}
